// src/lsp/lsp.zen
// The language server, and the folder's surface. `DESIGN.md:45`: "a thin
// server over compiler internals" — nothing here answers a question about
// Zen itself; a missing query belongs in `src/sema/` or `src/std/ast/`.
//
//   lsp_pos.zen        the wire's coordinates and this language's
//   lsp_json.zen       JSON as a value, an arena, and the writer
//   lsp_json_read.zen  JSON in
//   lsp_frame.zen      Content-Length framing
//   lsp_decl.zen       which declared name a position is inside — a
//                      re-export; the finder itself is std/ast/ast_named.zen
//   lsp_uri.zen        a document URI, as a path the compiler can open
//   lsp_hover.zen      hover: the type under the cursor
//   lsp_def.zen        definition: where the name was declared
//   lsp_symbol.zen     documentSymbol: a module's declarations, flat
//   lsp_compl.zen      completion: the candidate set at a position
//   lsp_colour.zen     semanticTokens: colour, from the lexer, and from
//                      the checker where it settled a name
//   lsp_names.zen      the semantic half: which names a clean build
//                      settled, read off the checker's memos
//   lsp_built.zen      the one build a session keeps, and the arena it
//                      dies by — shared by the settle and the queries
//   lsp_diag.zen       publishDiagnostics: when to build, which file,
//                      how an answer is taken back
//   lsp_fmt.zen        formatting: the buffer through `src/fmt/`, as one
//                      whole-document edit — never a second formatter
//   lsp_reply.zen      the wire's shapes: a request's fields read, a
//                      reply built
//   lsp_serve.zen      lifecycle, the overlay, and the dispatch table
//   lsp_stdio.zen      the pipe: frames in on stdin, frames out on stdout
//
// WHICH REQUESTS ARE ANSWERED, which are refused `-32601`, and which of
// the refusals are deliberate rather than merely unwritten: the table in
// `docs/design_lsp.md` §2, which is where that state is kept.
//
// WHAT AN ANSWER COSTS is the one thing that table does not collect, and
// it is what a reader of this folder trips over. Hover, definition and
// build-backed completion need a BUILD (~1s) and go quiet without one.
// documentSymbol, formatting and colour's LEXICAL half need only the
// buffer, so they answer on one that has never been saved; the first and
// the last also answer on a buffer that does not PARSE — which is why VS
// Code gets colour from this server at all — while formatting is the one
// that must not, and says so with `[]` rather than an error. Diagnostics
// are all three phases or nothing: type errors never show while syntax
// errors go unreported.

WirePos*, LineRun*, Step*, to_pos*, to_wire*, run_of*, step_at* = lsp.lsp_pos
write_wire*, write_range*, write_whole*, wire_at*, units_of* = lsp.lsp_pos
JsonId*, Run*, Pair*, Json*, Jsons*, write_text*, whole_of* = lsp.lsp_json
JsonFault*, Reader*, read*, push_utf8*, byte_of* = lsp.lsp_json_read
Envelope*, FrameFault*, frame_at*, write_frame*, write_decimal* = lsp.lsp_frame
short_by* = lsp.lsp_frame
Tell*, TypeAt*, ValueAt*, told_at*, is_nothing* = lsp.lsp_decl
Hover*, hover_at*, hover_in*, hover_with*, no_type* = lsp.lsp_hover
Target*, Defn*, definition_at*, definition_in* = lsp.lsp_def
definition_with*, no_target*, write_location* = lsp.lsp_def
Sym*, symbols_at*, write_symbols* = lsp.lsp_symbol
write_edits* = lsp.lsp_fmt
Item*, Trigger*, DUMMY*, complete_at*, complete_in* = lsp.lsp_compl
complete_shared*, sort_items*, write_items* = lsp.lsp_compl
FILE_SCHEME*, path_of*, uri_at* = lsp.lsp_uri
Built* = lsp.lsp_built
Spot*, Diagnostics*, Shared*, publish*, ERROR* = lsp.lsp_diag
write_capabilities*, SEMANTIC_TOKENS* = lsp.lsp_reply
Colour*, Classed*, index_of*, name_of*, colour_of* = lsp.lsp_colour
write_legend*, write_tokens*, sort_classes* = lsp.lsp_colour
classify* = lsp.lsp_names
Server*, serve* = lsp.lsp_serve
frame_byte*, frame_why* = lsp.lsp_serve
Drain*, serve_stdio* = lsp.lsp_stdio
